- Files alice/bob created in the directory inherited group `research` (setgid) and the ACL entries — `getfacl` on a test file showed `user:alice:rwx`, `user:bob:rwx`, `group:research:rwx`, `other::---`
- alice read bob's file and vice versa; alice wrote into bob's subdirectory
- Subdirectories inherited the setgid bit and the full default ACL set, so inheritance continues down the tree
- `other::---` on the directory and inherited entries on contents keep non-research users out

